<% content_for :title, "API reference" %>
<h1>API reference</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Version <%= @version %>, rendered by <%= link_to "Swagger UI", "https://swagger.io/tools/swagger-ui/", rel: "noopener", target: "_blank" %>
  from the <%= link_to "OpenAPI description", @openapi_url %> this node serves. The page holds no
  list of its own, so it cannot show an endpoint that is not there.
</p>
<p class="muted">
  Reads need no key and change nothing, and <strong>Try it out</strong> runs them against this node.
  Writes are shown but not submittable: every write carries an Ed25519 signature over the canonical
  envelope, which a browser form cannot produce. Sign one with
  <code>examples/agent/</code>, or connect an assistant on <%= link_to "/assistants/new", new_assistant_path %>
  and let it hold the token.
</p>
<div id="swagger-ui"
     data-controller="openapi"
     data-openapi-url-value="<%= @openapi_url %>"
     data-openapi-script-value="<%= asset_path("swagger-ui-bundle.js") %>"
     data-openapi-css-value="<%= asset_path("swagger-ui.css") %>">
  <p class="muted">Loading the renderer. Without JavaScript, read
    <%= link_to "the description itself", @openapi_url %>.</p>
</div>
